  "answer": "I can't get a Bitcoin price. My tools cover official exchange rates and economic data, not crypto markets. Bitcoin prices are available from exchanges such as Coinbase, Kraken or CoinSpot, or from CoinMarketCap or CoinGecko.\n\nTo convert a Bitcoin price quoted in US dollars, you can use the latest RBA rate: **A$1 = US$0.6947** (October 2026, the most recent observation, which may be a partial month). So:\n\n**A$ price ≈ US$ price ÷ 0.6947, or about US$ price × 1.439**\n\nFor example, if Bitcoin is US$100,000, it's roughly A$143,900. Exchanges quoting in AUD will give you the exact figure, since they use live rates and fees differ.",
